// PARAM: --analysis interval
// No verdict annotations: a parse-rejection case. A procedure declared `void`
// yields no value, so `return e` in its body has nowhere to deliver e: a call
// to it carries no destination. A bare `return` is the void form and stays
// legal (see 01-bare_return.vimp).
void p(int32 n) {
  return n
}
void main() {
  p(1)
}
